# {{NAME}}

Scaffolded by `aos artifact new`. A self-contained page over the coilyco kit.

    npm install
    npm run dev     # esbuild dev server
    npm run build   # emits dist/
    npm run check   # prettier, the same thing CI should run

## The page is the canvas

`body` carries `k-canvas k-canvas--auto` rather than nesting a canvas inside a
body with its own ground, which would land two fills on one surface. `--auto`
answers the viewer's default theme state, which stamps no attribute at all and
leaves `prefers-color-scheme` as the only signal.

## The vendored kit and its pin

`vendor/coilyco-kit.css` is a compiled build artifact of the website repo,
copied in and committed. Nothing here fetches styling, fonts or scripts at
runtime. `vendor/` is in `.prettierignore`: reformatting it would rewrite bytes
nobody here owns.

`aos artifact check` compares `vendor/coilyco-kit.json`'s **hash** against the
kit the running `aos` ships, and verifies the stylesheet against the
`css_sha256` that pin records, so an edited or deleted vendor copy fails rather
than passing on a sidecar nobody edits by hand. The two obvious alternatives are both wrong. A
**count** has false negatives, because swapping one literal for another leaves
every count identical while the tokens change, which is the exact case the pin
exists to catch. A **byte diff** of the compiled CSS has false positives,
because a formatting-only commit rewrites bytes and changes nothing semantic.

## Formatting

Keep `npm run check` and CI running the same formatter, or the suite passes
locally and fails on formatting.
